# Keeps build contexts small and — more importantly — keeps local
# credentials out of them. Applies to every image built from the repo
# root: ml (docker/ml.Dockerfile), web (apps/web/Dockerfile), and api
# (apps/api/Dockerfile).

# Local environment files. Never in a build context, at ANY depth.
# (docs/PROJECT_PLAN.md §7.1, docs/security/secrets-matrix.md)
#
# The `**/` prefix is load-bearing and must not be dropped. Docker matches
# these patterns against the path relative to the context root, so a bare
# `.dev.vars` excludes only a file of that name at the root — it would NOT
# exclude `apps/api/.dev.vars`, which is where the service-role key
# actually lives. Both app images `COPY . .` from the repository root, and
# CI exports every intermediate build layer to a shared cache
# (`cache-to: type=gha,mode=max`), so a miss here puts real credentials in
# a cache other jobs can read.
#
# Verify after editing this file:
#   docker build -f apps/api/Dockerfile --target build -t ctx-check .
#   docker run --rm ctx-check find / -name ".dev.vars" -not -path "*/node_modules/*"
# Expected output: nothing.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars.*
!**/.dev.vars.example

# Installed and derived output. Every image installs and builds from
# source inside the container; a host node_modules would also be the
# wrong platform.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-node
**/.turbo
**/.wrangler

# Test output
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/playwright/.cache

# VCS, CI, editor, and OS noise
.git
.gitignore
.github
.devcontainer
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Large local ML data (DVC-tracked, gitignored) and throwaway notebooks —
# bind-mounted at run time when needed, never baked into a layer.
ml/data
ml/notebooks

# Docs and planning scratch space are never shipped in an image.
docs
temp
